Subject: [PATCH 40/69] docs: add state authorization rule to AGENTS.md

All data in contract state must be cryptographically authorized at
insertion time. Deltas must include authorization data (e.g., member
entries with invite chains) alongside the data they authorize, rather
than relaxing verification to accept unverified data.

Prompted by PR #146 where "defense-in-depth" changes would have
accepted unverified messages from non-members.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
